    "statusMod.title": "ClaudeRipple mod",
    "statusMod.help": "Shows the ClaudeRipple status bar above the Claude Code prompt. It adjusts the reasoning effort to fit each prompt, assigns a suitable worker and effort to tasks delegated with ripple:auto, and keeps the prompt cache warm. It shows context usage, cache time left, plan limits and the latest routing path, and the Log menu shows the request log. Change the details from the bar's ⚙ icon or the `/ripple` command. Changes apply to sessions started after this.",
    "statusMod.saved": "Settings saved. They apply to Claude Code sessions started from now on.",
    "workerTools.help": "Gives workers generated by ClaudeRipple only tools for reading and editing files, running commands, searching, and using skills. Excluding the session's MCP servers and plugin tools from each worker request greatly reduces input token usage, but these workers cannot use external tools such as browsers or the iOS Simulator. If a worker needs those tools, define it yourself in an agent file in ~/.claude/agents. ClaudeRipple does not modify user-written agent files. Applies to new sessions.",
