    "mod.subtitle": "Set how the ClaudeRipple status bar in Claude Code picks the effort, delegates tasks to workers and keeps the prompt cache warm. Changes save immediately, and you can set the same options in the status bar's ⚙ panel.",
    "mod.saved": "Saved",
    "mod.conflict": "These settings were changed elsewhere. The latest settings have been loaded; make your change again.",
    "mod.offNotice": "The mod is currently off. These settings won't apply until you turn it on in {clients}.",
    "mod.openSettings": "ClaudeRipple mod settings",
    "mod.takesOverHelp": "When a job is big, Claude splits it up and delegates parts to subagents: helper AIs that work on their own. Unless told otherwise, Claude Code's built-in general-purpose subagent does the work. It runs on the same model as your current chat, so its usage counts against your plan at the same rate.",
    "mod.takesOverHelp2": "With ‘ripple:auto’, ClaudeRipple assigns the model only for tasks Claude delegates to ripple:auto. Tasks that call a worker by name run unchanged. With ‘All spawns’, tasks delegated to the default general-purpose subagent also switch to a model and effort that fit the task. ClaudeRipple checks tasks that name a specific model too: they run on that model only when they cite the user's explicit instruction or a written rule as the reason, and are refused otherwise. If you're not sure which to choose, we recommend ‘All spawns’.",
    "mod.notUsable": "Signed out or out of quota",
    "mod.jevKeyNote": "The TypeSafe API key is not stored here. Set it in the ⚙ panel of the Claude Code status bar, with the TYPESAFE_API_KEY environment variable, or in ~/.config/jev/.env.",
    "mod.zenAdd": "Add OpenCode Zen, which supports jev models, in Providers.",
    "mod.workersBlurb": "Delegated tasks are handled by worker models connected through ClaudeRipple. The main chat only delegates the work; ClaudeRipple judges its difficulty (low, medium, high or max) and runs it with the model and effort assigned to that worker.",
    "mod.models": "Models to use",
    "mod.modelsHelp": "The four workers use only the selected models. Workers without a specific model are assigned one from the selected models automatically.",
    "mod.fourWorkers": "The four workers",
    "mod.retired": "The former per-field settings and Auto (experimental) have been retired and merged into the four-worker setup.",
